From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:30:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] movies: decode one picture ahead on a helper thread, and a
 NEON YCbCr to RGBA row conversion

open_async(): decode() hands the unit to a thread of its own and returns the previous unit's picture, so the decoder works while the
caller converts and shows the last one. DecodeThreadPlatform lets a platform supply its own thread and event (the Vita pins it to a
spare core); <prefix>_MOVIE_ASYNC=0 turns it off. yuv420_row_to_rgba (movie/yuv_convert.hpp) replaces the per-pixel loop with the
same integer arithmetic, eight pixels at a time with NEON; tests/yuv_convert_tests.cpp compares it with the old loop for every
(y, cb, cr) in both ranges and random rows of every length. The test is one file, not a CMake target:
  g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Ihost -Iinclude tests/yuv_convert_tests.cpp -o yuv_test && ./yuv_test

Verified: on x86-64 the test reports 33,638,225 pixels with 0 mismatching rows (that is the scalar path). Not verified: the NEON
path, the speed-up and the intro movie on the PS Vita.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

